    "create_time": 1784082626.132,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "**Neighborhoods for a room at ~$1,800 (realistic options):**\n- **Inner Sunset / Inner Richmond:** quieter, foggier, good food, N-Judah / buses. Rooms often $1,400–1,900.\n- **Mission / Bernal Heights edge:** sunny, lively, BART access. Rooms $1,500–2,000; more competitive.\n- **Lower Haight / NoPa:** central, walkable, rooms often slightly above budget.\n- **Dogpatch / Potrero Hill:** sunnier, near Caltrain; fewer rooms listed.\n- **SoMa:** central but uneven block to block; check the exact street.\n\nPick based on where the incubator is. A 20-minute commute in SF is very different by neighborhood depending on transit lines.\n\n**Avoiding scams (very common in SF sublets):**\n1. **Never pay before seeing the place**, in person or a live video tour where they open doors/turn on the tap at your request.\n2. Red flags: owner \"abroad,\" asks for wire/Zelle/crypto/gift cards, price far below market, refuses a call.\n3. Verify the person has the right to sublet: ask for their lease or a landlord contact.\n4. Reverse-image-search the photos.\n5. Use a written sublease agreement with dates, rent, deposit and move-out terms.\n6. Pay the deposit by a method with a trail, and only after signing."
     ]
    },
